schema: encyclopedia-entry
object:
  title: Social Tokens for Creators
  type: encyclopedia-entry
  page_type: guide
  summary: >-
    A short guide to social tokens (community-specific tokens for
    membership, access, or reputation) covering the three main types
    (creator, community, reputation tokens), use cases for local regen
    nodes (event access, governance weight, incentive alignment, community
    identity), and pitfalls (over-financializing relationships, designing
    for speculation, securities-law exposure).
  audience: creators and local-node community organisers considering social tokens
  known_tensions:
    - >-
      The guide encourages using tokens to "track and reward contribution"
      while simultaneously warning against financializing community
      relationships and against designing for speculation — a tension it
      names but does not resolve with concrete guardrails.
  related_concepts:
    - social-token
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/social-tokens-creator.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  notes: >-
    assessed-but-excluded: article is short (60 lines) with no named
    external tools, no people/location/TEK/MRV content, and no specific
    funding/legal recommendation beyond a generic pointer to consult
    securities-law considerations — not treated as high_risk since it is a
    caution flag, not advice given. No resource-schema candidate produced;
    the article names no specific external tool/platform to register as a
    resource.
